  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "From the state Housing Element Annual Progress Report, through 2025.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001106",
        "SRC-001102"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CTCAC CA-22-462: Mainline North Apartments located at 2310 Calle Del Mundo in Santa Clara, requested and is being recommended for a reservation of $3,427,750 in annual federal tax credits to finance the new construction of 150 units of housing serving tenants with rents affordable to households earning 30-70% of area median income (AMI). Recorded as a note because this funding covers Mainline North Apartments (151 units), which may be one component of this record.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001621"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "These parties come from the 151-unit affordable building at 2310 Calle Del Mundo, which this record merges with the Ensemble building. ZAEN is the original project developer per the report.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001724"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Split: Parkside (2301 Calle Del Mundo, 301 market-rate units) now has its own record. CTCAC lists APN 097-46-024 for Mainline North, not in county data.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001603",
        "SRC-001914"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CalHFA (Nov 2022): the land, held by USA BH 26, Inc. after a 2020 purchase from 2302 Calle Del Mundo, LLC, was under a 9/1/2021 purchase agreement to Life Span Home, Inc. for $9,652,500, funded by contributions from Related ($6,425,000) and Ensemble ($3,227,500); Life Span leases the land back to the borrower for 99 years.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002760"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City of Santa Clara (2022): the project fulfills the consolidated inclusionary obligations of three Tasman East Specific Plan projects (Related California and Ensemble); proposed developer fee $9.387 million, of which $5,992,156 deferred; no direct city subsidy beyond the $6 million Related contribution loaned through the city at 0%.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001724"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ensemble press release (2023-04-17) lists financing partners Bank of America, CalHFA, City of Santa Clara, Google, Housing Trust Silicon Valley, Ensemble and Related, without amounts.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002762"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CalHFA construction sources total $83,055,810; permanent sources total $88,227,829. Construction lender Bank of America; supportive services by LifeSTEPS for 15 years.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002760"
      ]
    }
  ],
